<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dole</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dole, Jura</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dole is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doubs">Doubs</a> in the Jura <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, formerly the capital of the Free County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. It housed the county's parliament and, from 1422, its university. It fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> in 1668 and again in 1674, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besancon">Besançon</a> replaced it as capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-pasteur">Louis Pasteur</a> was born there in 1822.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dole.jpg" alt="Dole" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cjulien21 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dole_quartier_des_tanneurs.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
